From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:10:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: do not upload table 9 on FEM and HGPA
 boards

On a Netgear R6400 v1 (BCM4331, BFL_HGPA) the table 9 upload costs about
10 dB of TX power: a client close by receives the access point at -37 to
-44 dBm instead of -28 to -33 dBm, and the download drops from 109-111 to
68-70 Mbit/s. On an R6400 v2 (BFL_FEM) it makes no difference.

Read back from the hardware while Broadcom's wl driver runs, the R6400 v1
has table 9 at 0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 2, 3, ..., which is what b43 has without
the upload. Skip the upload on boards with an external front end
(BFL_FEM or BFL_HGPA).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_phy_ht.c
@@ -843,7 +843,9 @@ void b43_phy_ht_tables_init(struct b43_w
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(b43_httab_0x1a_0xc0_late_5g) !=
 			B43_HTTAB_1A_C0_LATE_SIZE);
 
-	httab_upload(dev, B43_HTTAB16(0x09, 0), b43_httab_0x09);
+	/* wl leaves table 9 at 0, 1, 2, 3, ... on FEM/HGPA boards (R6400) */
+	if (!(dev->dev->bus_sprom->boardflags_lo & (B43_BFL_FEM | B43_BFL_HGPA)))
+		httab_upload(dev, B43_HTTAB16(0x09, 0), b43_httab_0x09);
 	httab_upload(dev, B43_HTTAB16(0x12, 0), b43_httab_0x12);
 	httab_upload(dev, B43_HTTAB16(0x27, 0), b43_httab_0x27);
 	httab_upload(dev, B43_HTTAB16(0x26, 0), b43_httab_0x26);
